item.text:
I can assess privilege risk, but no report is present in the workspace. Please attach or paste it—ideally with identifiers redacted.

Also tell me:

- jurisdiction (state/territory and country);
- public or private health service;
- who commissioned the report, for what stated purpose, and whether a lawyer was involved;
- who prepared, received, or circulated it;
- whether it was created under a statutory protected-quality-assurance scheme; and
- whether litigation or a regulatory investigation was anticipated at the time.

An “RCA,” “confidential,” or “prepared for quality improvement” label does not by itself make a report privileged. The main possibilities are legal professional privilege, litigation privilege, and any jurisdiction-specific statutory protection. Circulation outside the necessary confidential group can also create waiver risk.

Until this is reviewed, restrict further distribution, preserve the original and its commissioning correspondence, and do not add a privilege label retrospectively without legal approval. I can provide an issue-spotting assessment once you supply the document; your organisation’s lawyer should make the final determination.
